From 58ad79b7a0c597a7f77e561894a7567b195b7a37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eileenthg <40307498+eileenthg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:22:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] WIP: port datagen providers (recipes, loot, tags,
 models, lang) to NeoForge 1.21.1

- DelightfulPlacementModifiers: RegistryObject -> DeferredHolder, package renames.
- DelightfulRecipeProvider (942 lines): buildRecipes(Consumer<FinishedRecipe>) ->
  buildRecipes(RecipeOutput) matching the vanilla 1.20.2+ RecipeOutput refactor;
  RecipeProvider's constructor now needs a CompletableFuture<HolderLookup.Provider>.
  ConditionalRecipe (removed entirely in NeoForge) replaced with
  RecipeOutput#withConditions(ICondition...) at each wrap()/cabinet()/knife()/
  knifeSmeltAndBlast() call site; IConditionBuilder/ICondition moved package only
  (net.minecraftforge.common.crafting.conditions -> net.neoforged.neoforge.common.conditions)
  with identical method names, so DSL call sites (not(), and(), tagEmpty(), modLoaded(),
  itemExists()) needed no changes. The one two-branch ConditionalRecipe usage
  (farmersdelight:chocolate_pie override) was simplified to a single conditioned override,
  relying on FD's own bundled recipe as the natural fallback when the condition is false
  (documented inline).
- DelightfulBlockLoot/DelightfulBlockTagProvider/DelightfulEntityTagProvider/
  DelightfulBlockStateProvider/DelightfulItemModelProvider/DelightfulLanguageProvider:
  RegistryObject -> DeferredHolder, ForgeRegistries -> BuiltInRegistries, provider packages
  moved to net.neoforged.neoforge.*. BlockLootSubProvider's constructor now needs a
  HolderLookup.Provider (matching FD's own FDBlockLoot pattern) - DelightfulBlockLoot and
  Generators' LootTableProvider wiring updated accordingly. Fixed a lingering
  `new ResourceLocation(...)` call in DelightfulItemModelProvider (removed public
  constructor) to ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath.
- Generators.java: @Mod.EventBusSubscriber -> top-level @EventBusSubscriber; threaded
  CompletableFuture<HolderLookup.Provider> lookup through every provider constructor that
  now needs one, matching FarmersDelight's own DataGenerators.java as ground truth.

Remaining: DelightfulItemTagProvider.java (1083 lines) is the last file with
net.minecraftforge imports.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
